redistributed inside the control binary.

Linux uses the distribution's NFS-Ganesha and VFS packages (LGPL-3.0-or-later
and their component licenses), and nfs-common (GPL-2.0-or-later and component
licenses). They are not statically linked into the control binary. The Linux
engine image retains package copyright/license records in /usr/share/doc and
copies engine notices to /usr/share/autobyteus-nfs/licenses. Its full package
inventory is /usr/share/autobyteus-nfs/packages.txt. Source packages are available
from the configured Ubuntu archive using the recorded exact package versions.

The Ubuntu base image and package dependencies retain their respective
licenses and notices. Release evidence records its immutable digest; do not
represent AutoByteus's license as relicensing those operating-system packages.
